# Sublime Pantry — environment variables.
#
# NONE of these may ever be referenced from client-side code or committed with
# real values. Set them in Netlify (Site configuration → Environment variables).
# Astro only exposes variables prefixed with PUBLIC_ to the browser; none here
# use that prefix, by design.

# --- Shopify Admin API ---
# Read by netlify/functions/lead-capture.mjs, scripts/check-shopify-title.mjs
# and scripts/create-webhooks.mjs. Scopes: read_customers + write_customers for
# the lead bridge, read_products for the title monitor, write_products +
# read_inventory for the webhook setup.
#
# THESE ARE THE ONLY SPELLINGS. Nothing reads SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN or
# SHOPIFY_ADMIN_TOKEN any more. The scripts used to accept both, which sounds
# forgiving and is not: a value set under the name a given file does not read
# fails identically to a value never set, and that is the failure this repo
# keeps finding weeks late. The GitHub repo secrets carry these same names, so
# there is no mapping anywhere to drift out of step.
SHOPIFY_SHOP_DOMAIN=zd-store-01m146jmxxhw739y7t7y11s669-paky1ta3.myshopify.com

# PREFERRED — client credentials grant.
# Shopify retired admin-created custom apps on 2026-01-01, so there is no token
# to copy out of the Shopify admin any more. Create an app in the Dev Dashboard
# (https://dev.shopify.com/dashboard), set the scopes on a released version,
# install it on the store, then copy the app's Client ID and Client secret.
# The function exchanges them for a 24h token at runtime and caches it.
# Requires the app and store to be in the SAME Shopify organization, otherwise
# Shopify returns `shop_not_permitted` — use the fallback below in that case.
SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# FALLBACK — a long-lived Admin API token, if you have one.
# Covers a legacy admin-created custom app, or a custom-distribution app
# installed via the authorization code grant. Takes precedence when set.
SHOPIFY_ADMIN_API_TOKEN=

# --- Netlify build hook (scripts/create-webhooks.mjs) ---
# The build hook for `main`, which the Shopify product/inventory webhooks call
# so the static site rebuilds when the catalog moves. Netlify → Site
# configuration → Build & deploy → Build hooks.
NETLIFY_BUILD_HOOK_URL=

# --- Judge.me (build-time only: src/lib/reviews.ts) ---
# Judge.me Admin → Settings → Integrations → View API tokens.
# Use the PRIVATE token. It is read at build time in Node and never shipped.
# Leave unset to build with no review section (the current, correct state).
JUDGEME_SHOP_DOMAIN=zd-store-01m146jmxxhw739y7t7y11s669-paky1ta3.myshopify.com
JUDGEME_PRIVATE_TOKEN=

# --- Klaviyo (server-side only: netlify/functions/submission-created.mts) ---
# Klaviyo → Settings → Account → API keys → Create private API key.
# Scopes required: profiles:write, subscriptions:write. Nothing more.
# This is a PRIVATE key: it must never be given the PUBLIC_ prefix, referenced
# from client code, or committed with a value. Set it in Netlify under
# Site configuration → Environment variables, scoped to Functions, for all
# deploy contexts. Unset, the bridge logs an error and returns 500 rather than
# silently dropping a subscriber. See docs/KLAVIYO-SUBSCRIBER-BRIDGE.md.
KLAVIYO_PRIVATE_API_KEY=
